# Project Overview

This project demonstrates the design and simulation of a 12 V to 5 V buck converter.

Objectives:

- Design a DC-DC step-down converter
- Simulate operation using LTspice
- Analyze output voltage behavior
- Measure inductor current ripple
- Verify switching-node operation
- Document simulation results

Tools Used:

- LTspice
- GitHub
- KiCad 

Key Results:

- Output Voltage: 4.73 V
- Switching Frequency: 500 kHz
- Ripple Current: ~0.6 A peak-to-peak
- Low output voltage ripple

The project serves as my foundation for future PCB implementation and power electronics design work.
